  "_comment": "The core lexicon (docs/to-do.md item 8; docs/vocabulary.md is its schema doc + highlights). Source of truth for G3/S2/S3/S6's word lookups. Six arrays: `droppedPreps` (G3, machine-actionable) — {verb, prep, ruling: \"drop\"|\"keep\"|\"replace\", forward?: \"apply\"|\"flag\" (default apply; \"flag\" withholds the forward transform when a high-frequency competing reading exists, e.g. duration `wait for`), replacedBy? (names a phrasalVerbs.phrasal for `replace` rulings), rank?, note?, confidence?} — invariant: at most one `drop` ruling per verb. `phrasalVerbs` (S2, machine-actionable) — {phrasal, plain (the one single-word machine replacement), alternates? (report text only), separable? (recorded; v1 matches contiguous occurrences only), rank?, note?, confidence?}. `sensePreferences` (S3, doc-only — applying needs word-sense disambiguation, not even flagged) — {standard, sense, ruling: \"replace\"|\"keep\", woe, rank?, note?}. `collocations` (S6, doc-only — allowed pairings, not required; also carries G3's `keep` rulings for adjective/noun-selected prepositions) — {standard, woe, ruling: \"replace\"|\"keep\", alternates?, rank?, note?}. `falseFriends` (doc-only, L1-specific, grows per language pair) — {l1, looksLike, actualMeaning, note?}. `registerDefaults` (doc-only) — {concept, variants, default, rank?, note?}. `confidence` defaults to \"high\" when omitted; demote to \"low\" for a sweep addition that collides with legitimate spec/sample text.",

